== Prior Art

neohab imports HABPanel configurations, and each of HABPanel's seven themes has a port here
that follows the colours of the original. HABPanel is part of the openHAB project, was written
by Yannick Schaus and contributors, and is licensed under the Eclipse Public License 2.0.

The add-on's entry point is derived from HABPanel's. NeohabTile.java registers the start page
tile and serves the bundled web app the way HABPanelTile.java does, which is the pattern every
openHAB UI add-on follows. Both are under the same license.

* File: HABPanelTile.java, in bundles/org.openhab.ui.habpanel/src/main/java/org/openhab/ui/habpanel/internal/
* Author: Yannick Schaus and contributors to the openHAB project
* License: Eclipse Public License 2.0
* Source: https://github.com/openhab/openhab-webui

No other HABPanel code is used or included.

Weather forecasts, when a weather widget is configured to use them, come from Open-Meteo
(https://open-meteo.com/), which is not included in this add-on and is called only with the
location the user configured.

